        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "example_question",
            "normalized_html": "<p>What is the solution to the equation <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 6^x - 6^5= 0?]</span> </p>",
            "readable_text": "What is the solution to the equation [MATH: 6^x - 6^5= 0?]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>EXPLANATION</p>",
            "readable_text": "EXPLANATION",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>First, we isolate the term with the variable exponent by adding <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 6^5]</span> to both sides:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 6^{x} \u2212 6^{5}|= 0; 6^{x} \u2212 6^{5} + 6^{5}|= 0 + 6^{5}; 6^{x} \u2212 6^{5} + 6^{5}|= 0 + 6^{5}; 6^{x}|= 6^{5}]</span></p><p>Since both sides of the equation share the same base <span class=\"math\">[MATH: (6),]</span> we can equate the exponents. </p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 6^{x}|= 6^{5}; x|= 5]</span></p><p>Therefore, the solution is <span class=\"math\">[MATH: {\\color{blue}x} = {\\color{blue}5}.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "First, we isolate the term with the variable exponent by adding [MATH: 6^5] to both sides:\n\n[MATH: 6^{x} \u2212 6^{5}|= 0; 6^{x} \u2212 6^{5} + 6^{5}|= 0 + 6^{5}; 6^{x} \u2212 6^{5} + 6^{5}|= 0 + 6^{5}; 6^{x}|= 6^{5}]\n\nSince both sides of the equation share the same base [MATH: (6),] we can equate the exponents.\n\n[MATH: 6^{x}|= 6^{5}; x|= 5]\n\nTherefore, the solution is [MATH: {\\color{blue}x} = {\\color{blue}5}.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Example Prompt:\nWhat is the solution to the equation [MATH: 6^x - 6^5= 0?]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nFirst, we isolate the term with the variable exponent by adding [MATH: 6^5] to both sides:\n\n[MATH: 6^{x} \u2212 6^{5}|= 0; 6^{x} \u2212 6^{5} + 6^{5}|= 0 + 6^{5}; 6^{x} \u2212 6^{5} + 6^{5}|= 0 + 6^{5}; 6^{x}|= 6^{5}]\n\nSince both sides of the equation share the same base [MATH: (6),] we can equate the exponents.\n\n[MATH: 6^{x}|= 6^{5}; x|= 5]\n\nTherefore, the solution is [MATH: {\\color{blue}x} = {\\color{blue}5}.]"
      },
