        "title": "Changing the Base of an Expression",
        "key_prerequisites": [],
        "has_content_in_snapshot": true,
        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Let&#x27;s take a look at the following equation: </p>",
            "readable_text": "Let's take a look at the following equation:",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 5^x = 25]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: 5^x = 25]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>We can&#x27;t solve this equation straight off the bat because the two sides of the equation don&#x27;t share a common base.</p>",
            "readable_text": "We can't solve this equation straight off the bat because the two sides of the equation don't share a common base.",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>However, notice that <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 25]</span> can be written as a power of <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 5\\mathbin{:}]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "However, notice that [MATH: 25] can be written as a power of [MATH: 5\\mathbin{:}]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 25=5^2]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: 25=5^2]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Therefore, we can rewrite the equation as</p>",
            "readable_text": "Therefore, we can rewrite the equation as",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 5^x = 5^2.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: 5^x = 5^2.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Since both sides of the equation are now written as an exponential expression with a common base of <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 5,]</span> we can set the exponents equal to each other and solve:</p>",
            "readable_text": "Since both sides of the equation are now written as an exponential expression with a common base of [MATH: 5,] we can set the exponents equal to each other and solve:",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 5^{x}|= 5^{2}; x|= 2]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: 5^{x}|= 5^{2}; x|= 2]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>To check that the solution is correct, we plug <span class=\"math\">[MATH: x=2]</span> into the original equation:</p>",
            "readable_text": "To check that the solution is correct, we plug [MATH: x=2] into the original equation:",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\eqalign{\n5^{2} &amp;= 25 \\\n25 &amp;= 25 \\; {\\color{green}{\\checkmark}}\n}]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: \\eqalign{\n5^{2} &= 25 \\\n25 &= 25 \\; {\\color{green}{\\checkmark}}\n}]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Content:\nLet's take a look at the following equation:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: 5^x = 25]\n\nContent:\nWe can't solve this equation straight off the bat because the two sides of the equation don't share a common base.\n\nContent:\nHowever, notice that [MATH: 25] can be written as a power of [MATH: 5\\mathbin{:}]\n\nContent:\n[MATH: 25=5^2]\n\nContent:\nTherefore, we can rewrite the equation as\n\nContent:\n[MATH: 5^x = 5^2.]\n\nContent:\nSince both sides of the equation are now written as an exponential expression with a common base of [MATH: 5,] we can set the exponents equal to each other and solve:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: 5^{x}|= 5^{2}; x|= 2]\n\nContent:\nTo check that the solution is correct, we plug [MATH: x=2] into the original equation:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: \\eqalign{\n5^{2} &= 25 \\\n25 &= 25 \\; {\\color{green}{\\checkmark}}\n}]"
      },
