          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>First, we divide both sides of the equation by <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 2\\mathbin{:}]</span></p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 2 \u22c5 3^{x}|= 54; (2 \u22c5 3^{x})/(2)|= (54)/(2); (2 \u22c5 3^{x})/(2)|= 27; 3^{x}|= 27]</span></p><p>Now, we can rewrite <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 27]</span> as <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 3^3]</span> so that both sides have the same base:\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: 3^{x} = 3^{3}]</span>\nEquating the exponents, we get <span class=\"math\">[MATH: {\\color{blue}x}={\\color{blue}3}.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "First, we divide both sides of the equation by [MATH: 2\\mathbin{:}]\n\n[MATH: 2 \u22c5 3^{x}|= 54; (2 \u22c5 3^{x})/(2)|= (54)/(2); (2 \u22c5 3^{x})/(2)|= 27; 3^{x}|= 27]\n\nNow, we can rewrite [MATH: 27] as [MATH: 3^3] so that both sides have the same base:\n[MATH: 3^{x} = 3^{3}]\nEquating the exponents, we get [MATH: {\\color{blue}x}={\\color{blue}3}.]",
